VOLITIONAL_MOTOR_ACTION_VERBS
│   // Actions initiated consciously and executed via primary motor cortex
│
├── 1. WHOLE_BODY_MOVEMENT → Full-body locomotion or repositioning
│   ├── walk → move at a regular pace
│   ├── run → move faster than walking
│   ├── jump → push off ground into air
│   ├── hop → jump on one foot
│   ├── skip → step and hop alternately
│   ├── crawl → move on hands and knees
│   ├── climb → ascend using limbs
│   ├── slide → move smoothly along surface
│   ├── roll → turn over repeatedly
│   ├── tumble → fall end-over-end
│   ├── squat → bend knees to lower body
│   ├── stretch → extend muscles fully
│   ├── bend → lean forward/downward
│   └── crouch → stay low with bent legs
│
├── 2. POSTURAL_TRANSITIONS → Changing physical position
│   ├── get up → rise from sitting/lying
│   ├── stand up → assume upright stance
│   ├── sit up → raise torso from lying
│   ├── lie down → assume horizontal position
│   ├── rise → elevate oneself slowly
│   ├── kneel → rest on one or both knees
│   ├── balance → maintain stability
│   ├── steady → stabilize after movement
│   ├── lean → incline body to one side
│   └── turn around → rotate 360°
│
├── 3. ARM_HAND_FINGER_ACTIONS → Upper limb manipulation
│   ├── GRASPING & HOLDING
│   │   ├── grasp → take hold firmly
│   │   ├── hold → keep in hand
│   │   ├── squeeze → press together
│   │   ├── release → let go
│   │   └── pinch → grip between thumb and finger
│   │
│   ├── MOVING & POSITIONING
│   │   ├── lift → raise upward
│   │   ├── lower → bring down
│   │   ├── raise → elevate
│   │   ├── reach → extend toward something
│   │   ├── wave → move hand side-to-side
│   │   ├── point → direct finger at object
│   │   ├── gesture → use motion to communicate
│   │   └── face → orient toward direction
│   │
│   ├── TOOL USE & INTERACTION
│   │   ├── press → apply force (button)
│   │   ├── tap → touch lightly and quickly
│   │   ├── click → make short sound (mouse)
│   │   ├── twist → rotate
│   │   ├── rotate → spin around axis
│   │   ├── flip → turn over
│   │   ├── fold → bend paper/fabric
│   │   ├── unfold → open folded item
│   │   └── spin → whirl rapidly
│
├── 4. LEG_FOOT_ACTIONS → Lower limb motion
│   ├── kick → strike with leg/foot
│   ├── step → move one foot forward
│   ├── stomp → step heavily
│   ├── stamp → bring foot down hard
│   ├── shuffle → drag feet while walking
│   ├── march → walk formally in rhythm
│   ├── jog → run slowly for exercise
│   ├── pedal → operate bike pedals
│   ├── skate → glide on ice/wheels
│   ├── ski → glide on snow
│   ├── dance → move rhythmically
│   ├── tiptoe → walk on toes
│   └── stampede → rush forward as a group
│
├── 5. SPEECH_ARTICULATION_AND_FACIAL_EXPRESSION → Controlled facial/vocal actions
│   // Note: Only when done *intentionally*
│   ├── smile → curve mouth upward
│   ├── frown → lower eyebrows and mouth
│   ├── grimace → distort face (e.g., pain)
│   ├── wink → close one eye briefly
│   ├── nod → move head up/down (yes)
│   ├── shake head → move side-to-side (no)
│   ├── purse lips → press lips together tightly
│   ├── raise eyebrow → show surprise/doubt
│   ├── whistle → produce sound through lips
│   └── yawn → open mouth wide (if deliberate)
│
├── 6. OBJECT_MANIPULATION → Interacting with items
│   ├── WRITING & DRAWING
│   │   ├── write → form letters
│   │   ├── type → press keys
│   │   ├── draw → sketch lines
│   │   ├── paint → apply pigment
│   │   ├── erase → remove marks
│   │   └── cut → slice with tool
│   │
│   ├── BUILDING & ORGANIZING
│   │   ├── glue → join with adhesive
│   │   ├── stick → attach
│   │   ├── place → put in location
│   │   ├── set → arrange
│   │   ├── arrange → order intentionally
│   │   ├── stack → pile vertically
│   │   └── pile → heap loosely
│   │
│   ├── MOVING_OBJECTS
│   │   ├── carry → transport in hands
│   │   ├── drag → pull behind
│   │   ├── pull → exert force toward self
│   │   ├── push → exert force away
│   │   ├── throw → propel through air
│   │   ├── catch → intercept moving object
│   │   ├── drop → let fall
│   │   ├── toss → throw gently
│   │   └── launch → send out forcefully
│   │
│   └── PRECISION_ACTIONS
│       ├── tear → rip apart
│       ├── fold → crease material
│       ├── roll → wrap into cylinder
│       └── flip → reverse orientation
│
└── 7. TRANSPORTATION_AND_NAVIGATION → Controlling vehicles/movement systems
    ├── ride → travel on vehicle
    ├── drive → operate car
    ├── steer → control direction
    ├── pilot → fly aircraft
    ├── row → propel boat with oars
    ├── sail → travel by wind power
    ├── fly → operate aircraft
    ├── glide → descend smoothly
    ├── land → arrive safely on ground
    └── dock → secure vessel to pier
